# Pinned third-party payload pieces. Not vendored: bin/fetch-assets.sh fetches
# them into vendor/ and refuses anything whose sha256 does not match. To bump:
# edit the version (and the FILE, if it carries one), set the sha256 to SKIP,
# run `make vendor`, paste back the hash it prints.

# The stock FlashForge package -- the one input the build cannot synthesise,
# and the only pin here that is not a payload piece. ONE PER MODEL, and they
# are not interchangeable: each carries its own firmwareExe and refuses to
# install on the other, so bin/common.sh picks by TARGET_MACHINE.
#
# Nothing proprietary is redistributed from this repo. ghzserg/FF is the public
# archive docs/support.md already sends printer owners to for the undo button,
# and the sha256 is what makes building from somebody else's mirror safe: the
# archive can change under us and the build stops instead of quietly producing
# a package diffed against firmware nobody checked.
#
# THE TAG IS A ROLLING `R` holding every FlashForge model at once, so there is
# no per-release tag to move to -- the pin is the FILENAME plus the sha256, and
# the filename carries the version. A withdrawn asset breaks the fetch loudly.
#
# To build against firmware you downloaded yourself, set STOCK_TGZ_CREATOR5PRO
# (or _CREATOR5) in config.env. Unlike HELIX_TGZ that path is never overwritten
# -- see the note in bin/fetch-assets.sh for why this one is the exception.
STOCK_URL_BASE="https://github.com/ghzserg/FF/releases/download/R"
STOCK_VERSION="1.9.7-1.2.9-20260810"
STOCK_FILE_CREATOR5PRO="Creator5Pro-$STOCK_VERSION.tgz"
STOCK_SHA256_CREATOR5PRO="1f3252feaae6d8fc72d7b0fd1ba832cc63d369659f8b2d2896efcf7adab2976b"
STOCK_FILE_CREATOR5="Creator5-$STOCK_VERSION.tgz"
STOCK_SHA256_CREATOR5="72009be183e74a4562050a927787ba686c6b558a075f00958892197ac52659cc"

MAINSAIL_VERSION="v2.18.2"
MAINSAIL_SHA256="df2ba7c301f7bfc8ac9f122741a6ba08356d679ecfa1f62f898d0337802d5de5"

